  "note": "Full unchanged measured-source XYZ, not independent surveys or accuracy ground truth. Native PLY order is preserved and differs from browser LOD indexing. Full-input production Delaunay TIN uses automatic edge rejection without extra thinning or transformed/generated coordinates. Independent archived native baseline supplies complete f64 distance bits, six f64 statistics bits and scalar PLY oracle, then exits before timing. Separate baseline/candidate contexts use identical TIN, original 4096-point Morton query chunks and fixed Rayon thread count. Whole native cloud_to_mesh_par includes fresh BVH construction, Morton preparation/sorting, parallel queries, joining, BVH destruction and pool installation. Both builds keep adopted stack reuse, cached traversal bounds, indexed mesh preparation, bottom-up bounds and parallel tree construction enabled, with the rejected seed-triangle experiment disabled. Candidate parallelizes query-coordinate bounds and indexed key generation for at least 65536 points. Bounds use 16384-point chunks with finite-nonzero admission gathered during each chunk scan. Zero/nonfinite inputs recompute bounds in the original serial order to preserve target-dependent tie/NaN bits. Finite nonzero extrema preserve exact numeric/bit values when merged. Key generation preserves original per-point f64 arithmetic and saturating casts, and indexed Rayon collection preserves initial pair order. Key-only unstable sorting and index extraction remain serial and unchanged, including equal-key order. Queries are never repartitioned or rescheduled differently. Other native C2C/sequential/prepared/WASM/hinted APIs retain serial Morton preparation. Parallel scheduling, bound scratch allocation, admission and fallback work are included in timing. Chunk summaries are transient and dropped before key allocation; no new persistent geometry/query/result cache is introduced. Key/order capacities and downstream scratch remain unchanged. No peak process memory guarantee is made. Loading, meshing, pool construction, first use, five alternating warmups, f64/statistics/PLY serialization and verification and cleanup are excluded. Ten alternating timed pairs are retained without outlier removal. No builds/tests/scans/edits run alongside timing. Archived sources, executables, compiler, script, inputs/manifests/original PCD are checked before/after. Clocks, power, scheduling, other applications, allocator, code layout and retained pages are uncontrolled. No isolated ordering, Python conversion, C2C, browser, WASM or GPU speedup claim. No GPU model identifiers collected."
